      "body": "…em path\n\nThe AllGatherGEMMPattern replacement calls fused_all_gather_matmul but never uses the gathered tensor (ag_output). However, it relies on the default return_A=True, which prevents the multimem execution path in _should_use_multimem_all_gather_matmul from being selected.\n\nSetting return_A=False signals that the gathered tensor is not needed, enabling the NVLink multicast-based multimem path for small M values. Microbenchmarks on 8xH100 show 1.5x-8.5x per-op speedup for M<=2048.\n\nNote: PyTorch's native Inductor FX pass (micro_pipeline_tp.py) already performs this optimization by checking if ag_output has no downstream users, but vLLM's pattern matcher does not do this liveness analysis.\n\n<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Purpose\n\n## Test Plan\n\n## Test Result\n\n---\n<details>\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\n- [ ] (Optional) Release notes update. If your change is user facing, please update the release notes draft in the [Google Doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YyVqrgX4gHTtrstbq8oWUImOyPCKSGnJ7xtTpmXzlRs/edit?tab=t.0).\n</details>\n\n",
